# Allowlist, not a denylist.
#
# Everything is excluded first and the few paths the image actually needs
# are added back. A denylist protects exactly the files someone thought of
# on the day they wrote it, and silently starts shipping whatever gets
# added to the repository root afterwards -- which, in a repository whose
# root already holds a .env, is the wrong default to pick.
*

!app
!requirements.txt

# Re-excluded inside the allowed paths above: build artefacts are rebuilt
# by the interpreter and would otherwise bust the layer cache on every
# build and ship stale bytecode compiled by a different interpreter.
app/**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Named explicitly for the reader, though `*` above already excludes them.
# These are the paths that must never reach an image: local secrets, the
# developer virtualenv (Windows binaries, useless and large in a Linux
# image), version control history and test caches.
.env
.env.*
.venv
.git
.pytest_cache
